From 0c038f7580983f4272d597b1f87c72034688d09c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:53:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH stable 6.1] Revert "selftests/bpf: Update tests for new ct
 zone opts for nf_conntrack kfuncs"

This reverts the stable backport of upstream commit a87f34e742d2
("selftests/bpf: Update tests for new ct zone opts for nf_conntrack
kfuncs").

The commit was pulled into this stable branch solely as a Stable-dep-of
commit 5e8c349bc8d7 ("selftests/bpf: Fix flaky bpf_nf test when random
NAT port is 0"). However, it tests the ct_zone_id and ct_zone_dir fields
of struct bpf_ct_opts, which were introduced in v6.10 with commit
ece4b2969041 ("net: netfilter: Make ct zone opts configurable for bpf ct
helpers"), and that kernel-side change is not (and, being a new feature,
should not be) present here. As a result test_bpf_nf.bpf.o can no longer
be loaded, and bpf_nf/xdp-ct along with bpf_nf/tc-bpf-ct fail:

  ; opts_def.ct_zone_id = 10;
  386: <invalid CO-RE relocation>
  failed to resolve CO-RE relocation <byte_off> [138] struct bpf_ct_opts___new.ct_zone_id (0:4 @ offset 10)
  ...
  libbpf: prog 'nf_xdp_ct_test': failed to load: -22
  libbpf: failed to load object 'test_bpf_nf'
  libbpf: failed to load BPF skeleton 'test_bpf_nf': -22
  test_bpf_nf_ct:FAIL:test_bpf_nf__open_and_load unexpected error: -22

Drop the new ct zone opts tests, while preserving the part of the
flaky-test fix that applies to the pre-existing nf_ct_test().
